        "thought_text": "The optimal value of 'a' should be the median of the x-coordinates, not the y-coordinates. This is because the equation of the tram line is y = x + a, and we want to minimize the total unusefulness, which is the sum of squared distances from each point to the line. The median minimizes the sum of absolute deviations, which in this case leads to the minimum sum of squared deviations.",
